    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are pleased to present to the market 28 Wainsfort Manor Crescent. An attractive red brick, semi detached family home boasting a sunny garden to rear, off street parking and side entrance. Situated in a highly sought after development off Wainsfort Road within walking distance to Terenure village and Bushy Park.\r\n\r\nThis impressive property offers spacious well-proportioned accommodation of approximately 97 SqM and briefly comprises of entrance hallway with understairs storage and guest w.c off. Well appointed living room to the front with gas fire, ceiling coving and box bay window. Beyond the hallway and through double doors off the living room is the open plan kitchen/ dining, the kitchen itself has an extensive range of shaker style kitchen units, extractor fan, plumbed for dishwasher and washing machine and door to garden, additionally there are sliding doors to the garden off the dining area. \r\n\r\nUpstairs is equally as impressive with 3 generously sized bedrooms (master ensuite). Bedroom 1 is to the rear with built in wardrobes and fully tiled ensuite shower room off. Bedrooms 2 and 3 are to the front, both with built in wardrobes. The family bathroom completes the internal accommodation with shower, w.c, whb and fully tiled. \r\n\r\nOutside to the front is a cobblocked area for off street parking with mature shrubs and trees.  To the rear is a sunny private garden, laid out in lawn bordered with mature planning and trees with a paved patio area and side entrance. \r\n\r\nWainsfort Manor is a much sought after and well established development off Wainsfort Road with every amenity within walking distance. There are excellent sporting facilities in and around Terenure including swimming facilities, numerous rugby clubs, tennis clubs and GAA clubs. Bushy Park which hosts a weekly markets and the village is known for its excellent range of shopping from large supermarkets to smaller artisan providers as well as good restaurants and cafes. \r\nEducation is very well catered in the area with a host of both primary and secondary schools on your doorstep to include – St. Pius , St. Joseph's BNS, Presentation Primary School, Presentation College, Terenure College Templeogue College and Our Lady's Secondary school. The area provides quick and easy access to the M50 as well as the city centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall \r\nCeiling coving and understairs storage. \r\n\r\nGuest w.c, \r\nW.c, whb, tiled floor and part tiled walls.  \r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\nSolid wood flooring, ceiling coving, box bay window, gas fire with marble surround and double doors to \r\n\r\nOpen plan Kitchen/Dining \r\nKitchen \r\nRange of overhead and undercounter shaker style fitted units, plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher. 1 1/3 stainless steel sink unit, tiled floor, part tiled walls and door to garden. \r\n\r\nDining \r\nSolid wood flooring, sliding door to garden.   \r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\nBedroom 1 (Rear) Ensuite  \r\nBuilt in wardrobes. \r\nEnsuite \r\nFully tiled with walk in dual shower, recessed shelf, vanity whb, vanity light and mirror, glass shelving, w.c and towel radiator. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (Front) \r\nBuilt in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (Front) \r\nBuilt in wardrobe.  \r\n\r\nBathroom\r\nFully tiled, shower, w.c, vanity whb vanity light and mirror, glass shelf and towel radiator. \r\n\r\nLanding \r\nAccess to attic and hotpress. \r\n\r\nOutside \r\nThe front of the property is cobblock off street parking with mature hedges and trees. Side entrance.\r\nSunny garden to the rear laid out in lawn bordered by mature trees and shrubs throughout."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
